what is the General Secretariat of the  council also known as the GRC it is a  body of staff that supports two  institutions the European Council and  the Council of the EU as well as their  presidencies its role is to help  organize and ensure the coherence of the  council's work the GSC has a wide  variety of tasks it organizes and  supports over 4,000 meetings every year  at all levels from civil servants to  ministers to heads of state or  government it prepares the documents  needed before and after these meetings  including agendas reports or draft laws  it registers archives and translates  these documents it gives legal advice to  the institutions it serves and  communicates on their activities the GRC  also manages the budget for both  institutions which is around 0.4 percent  of the total EU budget to achieve all  this to the highest standard the GSC can  count on its 2,800 staff members coming  from all over the EU policy officers and  technical experts IT communicational  translation professionals work at all  levels in the different GSD departments  their work is based on the principles of  Independence and professionalism in at  least two official languages the GSC is  led by its secretary-general who is  appointed by the council find out more  about the GRC and much more on Concilium  zero / gu
 

